# class: install-guide
# schema: id | kind | summary | source
# source: docs/install.md
# recipe: novel
# authored: 2026-05-23
# reindexed: 2026-05-27 (flag matrix restructured: -LocalDb flag added; no-flag default changed to production/CI; SHA drift refresh)
# Recipe: per flag/prereq/stack-shape/migration/troubleshooting row extract id, kind (prereq / flag / stack-shape / migration / troubleshooting), one-line summary, source anchor.

flag-no-flag | flag | (no flag) production/CI default: app stack against external Postgres (ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection required); no fetcher, no demo services; fail-fast (exit 1) if connection string unset | @docs/install.md#flag-matrix-at-a-glance
flag-local-db | flag | -LocalDb (PowerShell) / --local-db (bash): starts bundled db container (--profile db + postgres:16-alpine); no fetcher; no demo; push events manually via POST /api/deployments; quick local eval without external Postgres | @docs/install.md#quick-start--local-evaluation-with-bundled-postgres
flag-real-gha | flag | -RealGha (PowerShell) / --real-gha (bash): real GitHub Actions upstream; requires $env:GHA_TOKEN; fetcher profile active; renamed from -Fetcher per CR-0013 | @docs/install.md#flag-matrix-at-a-glance
flag-empty | flag | -Empty (PowerShell) / --empty (bash): bare stack api+gateway+frontend+db; no fetcher; no demo-gha; direct POST /api/deployments integrators / power users | @docs/install.md#flag-matrix-at-a-glance
flag-demo-back-compat | flag | -Demo (PowerShell) / --demo (bash): back-compat alias; routes to default demo stack + logs one informational line; NOT documented in quick-start; will be removed after one release cycle | @docs/install.md#flag-matrix-at-a-glance
prereq-docker | prereq | Docker (Engine + Compose v2): runs the four release images (gateway/api/dashboard/fetcher) + postgres:16-alpine + deployment-dashboard-demo-gha under demo profile | @docs/install.md#prerequisites
prereq-gh-cli | prereq | gh CLI on PATH: replaces anonymous curl/irm; all asset fetches and GHCR image pulls flow through gh's authenticated session; gh auth status must return 0 | @docs/install.md#prerequisites
prereq-gh-packages-scope | prereq | gh token must carry read:packages, write:packages, or admin:packages (hierarchical — write includes read; default gh auth login does NOT include any); refresh with gh auth refresh --hostname github.com --scopes read:packages | @docs/install.md#prerequisites
quickstart-windows | stack-shape | Windows PowerShell 7+ two-step: gh release download install.ps1 + pwsh install.ps1; boots demo profile; dashboard on http://localhost:8080/ within ~60s; installer prints generated API_TOKEN once + persists to ./dashboard-release/dashboard.env | @docs/install.md#quick-start--demo-default-windows-powershell-7
quickstart-linux-mac | stack-shape | Linux/macOS bash two-step: gh release download install.sh + bash install.sh; same demo-default stack + URL | @docs/install.md#quick-start--demo-default-linux--macos
demo-what-you-see | stack-shape | Within ~60s: matrix >=20 slots (6 services × 5+ envs), >=5 box states, DAG edges (4 parent_deployments shapes), SSE events every 5-10s, zero outbound network calls (fetcher polls demo-gha in-network) | @docs/install.md#what-you-see
real-gha-usage | flag | -RealGha: GHA_TOKEN must be exported before install; two tokens are distinct (GHA_TOKEN = fetcher PAT for GH API; gh CLI token = Releases + GHCR auth); GHA_REPOSITORIES defaults to user value via dashboard.env round-trip | @docs/install.md#real-github-repos----realgha
version-pinning | flag | -Version v1.2.3 (PowerShell) / --version v1.2.3 (bash): pin installer to specific release tag; gh release download v1.2.3 fetches that tag's installer; docker-compose.release.yml images pin to DASHBOARD_VERSION=v1.2.3 | @docs/install.md#quick-start--demo-default-windows-powershell-7
migration-actuation | migration | No install-time migration step; API self-migrates on startup per ADR-0009; installer polls /health until healthy; healthy = migrations applied + serving; no -SkipMigrations flag, no migration.sql download, no --profile migrate | @docs/install.md#1-fetches-release-assets-from-github-via-gh-release-download
dashboard-env | stack-shape | installer writes ./dashboard-release/dashboard.env (POSTGRES_PASSWORD random hex + API_TOKEN random hex + ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection + DASHBOARD_VERSION); sourced by subsequent compose invocations; persists the generated API_TOKEN for CI/CD POSTs | @docs/install.md#what-you-see
custom-port | flag | -Port <N> (PowerShell) / --port <N> (bash): retargets ${DASHBOARD_PORT} in release compose; avoids host-port collision | @docs/install.md
uninstall | stack-shape | uninstall.ps1 / uninstall.sh: docker compose -f docker-compose.release.yml down + cleanup of install directory | @docs/install.md
migration-back-compat | migration | Pre-ADR-0009 installs shipped a 6th migration.sql release asset; current installer does NOT download it; upgrade v1.0.0->v1.2.0 transparent via docker compose pull + up -d (API carries new migrations; applies on startup) | @docs/install.md
